#
# The Python packages the Ansible collection's jobs and its tests install
# (.gitlab/ci/channels.yml's galaxy-check, galaxy-build and galaxy-publish;
# hmailserver/docs/Ansible.md), by hand-chosen version.
# build/ci/ansible-collection-requirements.txt is made from this file, with every
# package they pull in pinned and every file's SHA-256, and that is the file they
# install from (pip --require-hashes):
#
#   ansible        the community package: ansible-core (ansible-galaxy,
#                  ansible-playbook, ansible-test) with the collections the role
#                  uses beside ansible.builtin - community.general's ini_file and
#                  zypper - and community.docker, whose docker_container and
#                  connection the molecule scenarios start and reach their
#                  containers with
#   ansible-lint   the linter, in its production profile
#   molecule       the scenarios under the collection's extensions/molecule
#   docker         the Docker SDK community.docker's modules call
#
# To move a version, change it here and regenerate the pinned file with uv, from
# PyPI, --universal so that one file holds for the Linux jobs and a desk:
#
#   python -m venv /tmp/uv && /tmp/uv/bin/pip install uv
#   /tmp/uv/bin/uv pip compile --universal --generate-hashes --python-version 3.14 \
#       --output-file build/ci/ansible-collection-requirements.txt build/ci/ansible-collection-requirements.in
#
# then put this file's three header lines back at the top of the output.
ansible==14.5.0
ansible-lint==26.10.1
molecule==26.10.0
docker==7.2.0
